title: 'P14b-web passes on darwin: kernel-accept socket hand-off to a no-network transport child'
summary: 'Probe p14b-web-handoff: the kernel listens on 127.0.0.1 (pauseOnConnect) and hands each accepted socket via subprocess.send(''conn'', socket) to a sandbox-exec child with no network-* rule. 4 MiB both ways sha-verified (8 ms), client close seen, 5 repeated hand-offs, and all 13 child bind/listen (0.0.0.0, ::, en0, 127.0.0.1, ::1, no host), UDP bind, outbound TCP and unix connect attempts EPERM; unsandboxed control reached all 13.'
symbols_touched:
  - '#oracle-sandbox'
  - '#web-endpoint'
commit: 265e36bb
learnings:
  - SBPL needs no network rule to read/write an inherited connected socket
  - listen() with no host is denied too so the implicit-bind path is closed
